-- Short Description
------------------------
-- Tests Link Fault Signaling when the GEM is operated at 2.5G.
--
------------------------
-- Test Summary
------------------------
--   0. Misc setup and pin check.
--   1. Program the DUT, enable the LFSM and wait for PCS synchronization.
--   2. Receive <4 Faults of each type and check that the link status doesn't
--      change.
--   3. Receive >=4 Faults of each type and check that the link status does
--      properly change. Then, wait a sufficiently long time to make the status
--      clear to OK.
--   4. Transmit packets while receiving >=4 Faults of each type.
--   5. Some activity to hit holes in CC.
--   6. Force end of test in case it doesn't stop of its own accord.
--
------------------------
-- Detailed Description
------------------------
-- Link Fault Signaling is defined in IEEE 802.3 Clause 46.3.4 (10G). Amendment
-- 802.3bz extends this features for 2.5G and 5G. Link Fault Signaling takes
-- place in the inter-frame period as Sequence ordered sets.
-- The GEM gives an implementation of the Link Fault State Machine (LFSM) for
-- 2.5G in the PCS.
--
-- Sequence ordered sets are presented to the 2.5G PCS (IEEE 802.3cb) as:
--   /Q/ = /K28.5/W/K28.5/W/K28.5/W/K28.5/W/
--
-- The Sequence ordered sets for the different Link Statuses goes as per the
-- encoding/decoding functions defined in IEEE 802.3cb Clause 127.2:
--   Link OK           : /K28.5/D00.0/K28.5/D00.6/K28.5/D00.6/K28.5/D00.0/
--   Local Fault       : /K28.5/D00.0/K28.5/D00.6/K28.5/D16.6/K28.5/D00.0/
--   Remote Fault      : /K28.5/D00.0/K28.5/D00.6/K28.5/D00.7/K28.5/D00.0/
--   Link Interruption : /K28.5/D00.0/K28.5/D00.6/K28.5/D16.7/K28.5/D00.0/
--
-- When transalted to octects:
--   Link OK           : /0xbc /0x00 /0xbc /0xc0 /0xbc /0xc0 /0xbc /0x00 /
--   Local Fault       : /0xbc /0x00 /0xbc /0xc0 /0xbc /0xd0 /0xbc /0x00 /
--   Remote Fault      : /0xbc /0x00 /0xbc /0xc0 /0xbc /0xe0 /0xbc /0x00 /
--   Link Interruption : /0xbc /0x00 /0xbc /0xc0 /0xbc /0xf0 /0xbc /0x00 /
--
-- When the DUT receives >=4 Faults of the same type in a row, the link status
-- shall change to the particular type of fault. Adjacent faults can be
-- intermixed with non-fault ordered sets. The link status is cleared to OK
-- after receiveing 128 consecutive non-fault columns (i.e. 256 couple of code
-- groups).
-- When the link status is:
--   1. Local Fault, then the PCS Tx shall transmit Remote Fault /Q/,
--   2. Remote Fault or Link Interruption, then the PCS Tx shall transmit /I1/
--      or /I2/ ordered sets.
-- When the link status changes an interrupt is triggered (if enabled) and the
-- status itself can be read in the network_status register.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ************************************************************************** --
-- 0. Test misc setup and pin check.
-- ************************************************************************** --

-- Design configuration requirements
requires no_pcs             0    -- PCS shall be present
requires ext_fifo_interface 0    -- DMA shall be present
requires rx_pkt_buffer      1    -- DMA shall be of 'Packet Buffer' type
requires tx_pkt_buffer      1    -- DMA shall be of 'Packet Buffer' type

-- Disable txd checking for this test
set_tx_data_check 0;

-- Check the reset state of some DUT pins
pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1 extint 0 speed 0

-- ************************************************************************** --
-- 1. Program the DUT, enable the LFSM and wait for PCS synchronization.
--    The LFSM is enabled by writing:
--       a. pcs_control[12]     = 0 (enable_auto_neg)
--       b. network_config[31]  = 0 (uni_direction_enable)
--       c. network_config[11]  = 1 (pcs_select)
--       d. network_control[29] = 1 (two_pt_five_gig)
--    By default, the testbench drives automatically IDLE2 ordered sets (/I2/ =
--    /K28.5/D5.6/) into PCS Rx. A long stream would cause the PCS to become
--    synchronized. When auto-negotiation is disabled, the link status indicates
--    the PCS synchronization status.
-- ************************************************************************** --

-- Check the reset value of needed registers and enable interrupts
apbrd(100) 000 00000000        -- network_control : check reset
apbrd      008 00000006        -- network_status  : check reset
apbrd      024 00000000        -- int_status      : check reset
apbrd      200 00009040        -- pcs_control     : check reset
apbwr      028 00000200        -- int_enable      : enable link change interrupt

-- Initialize the DMA transmit queue pointers. This is needed to transmit some
-- packets later on in the test
init_q_ptr -num_tx_queues 1 -num_rx_queues 0

-- Enable LFSM: select 2.5G, disable auto-negotiation, select PCS and disable
-- unidirection. Also set Tx enable for later in the test
apbwr      000 20000008        -- network_control : 2.5G and Tx enable
apbwr      200 00000140        -- pcs_control     : disable auto-negotiation
apbwr      004 00080c02        -- network_config  : PCS and unidir disable

-- Wait for link status change to trigger an interrupt and check the
-- network_status reg to assert PCS synchronization
apbrd(int) 024 00000200        -- int_status     : check link_status interrupt
apbwr      024 00000200        -- int_status     : clear interrupt
apbrd      024 00000000        -- int_status     : readback
apbrd      008 00000007        -- network_status : check pcs_link_state

-- Wait some time by dummy reading the network_control reg and make the
-- testbench settle
apbrd      000 20000008 num=20 -- network_control : readback
apbrdf     000 20000008        -- network_control : readback

-- ************************************************************************** --
-- 2. Receive <4 Faults of each type and check that the link status doesn't
--    change.
-- ************************************************************************** --

-- Inject Local Fault /Q/ mixed with /I2/ into PCS Rx
pcs_synch_rx(apb) sbc o00 sbc oc0 sbc od0 sbc o00
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o00 sbc oc0 sbc od0 sbc o00
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o00 sbc oc0 sbc od0 sbc o00

-- Wait some time by dummy reading the network_control reg and make the
-- eventual link status change happen. Check that no interrupt is present and
-- that the status is OK
apbrd      000 20000008 num=20 -- network_control : readback
apbrd      024 00000000        -- int_status      : readback
apbrdf     008 00000007        -- network_status  : check link OK

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Inject Remote Fault /Q/ mixed with /I2/ into PCS Rx
pcs_synch_rx(apb) sbc o00 sbc oc0 sbc oe0 sbc o00
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
pcs_synch_rx      sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50 sbc o50
